  "name": "guided-tour",
  "description": "Guided tour of kcap for someone who has it installed but does not yet know what it does for them — \"what does kcap do for me\", \"what is kcap\", \"is this thing doing anything\", \"what can kcap do\", \"just installed kcap, now what\", \"give me a tour\", \"Start kcap guided tour\" (the prompt `kcap setup` tells them to type) — or when they invoke this skill directly by its listed name. Also recognizes the former name Capacitor, including \"what is Capacitor\" and \"Start Capacitor guided tour\". Seven short cards, one per reply: welcome, capture, investigate, collaborate, review, use, reuse — each a handful of questions to ask the coding agent. Offers to install kcap if it is not set up. Not for general session recall on an established user — that is the recap skill.",
